diff --git a/AGENTS.md b/AGENTS.md
index 5bb85dd..59bce93 100644
--- a/AGENTS.md
+++ b/AGENTS.md
@@ -151,3 +151,10 @@ rg -C2 -i 'speedway' lang/po/ko.po | rg -v '^(#:|--)' | head -n 20
 - When fixing a bug, preserve requested behavior and visible content unless the user explicitly asks to remove it; fix the underlying issue instead of suppressing the affected feature.
 - When reviewing PRs that stop tracking generated or externally pulled files, verify ignore rules by running the generator/pull command or checking `git status --ignored`; do not assume removed tracked files are ignored.
 - When generated or externally pulled files are removed from tracking, verify all CI and release consumers still receive required files or directories.
+
+## Highway foundation validation
+
+When editing highway mapgens, verify the central median at both north/south and east/west OMT seams. Pavement connectivity alone does not verify carriageway alignment. Render the JSON geometry and check two 15-square carriageways separated by the two guardrail squares, including rotated templates.
+Native mapgen tests must temporarily set `disable_mapgen = false` and restore it: `clear_all_state()` defaults to the generic test mapgen. Check an actual road edge or guardrail as well as pavement.
+
+Highway corridor finalization must run after forest trailheads as well as regular specials: trailhead placement can add local roads after `place_specials()`. Keep the complete-generation regression test; reserve/finalize unit tests alone do not cover these late connections.
